WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:21.829
Good morning! Who are you?

2
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.575
I'm a zebra.

3
00:00:25.576 --> 00:00:30.046
We're a lot like horses!

4
00:00:30.047 --> 00:00:32.838
Where do you live?

5
00:00:32.839 --> 00:00:37.833
We live in Africa.

6
00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:43.624
We like grasslands and woodlands.

7
00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:49.931
I like your black and white stripes!

8
00:00:49.932 --> 00:00:53.562
All zebras have stripes.

9
00:00:53.563 --> 00:00:59.309
But every zebra's stripes look different.

10
00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.074
What do you eat?

11
00:01:02.075 --> 00:01:05.626
We graze.

12
00:01:05.627 --> 00:01:10.296
That means we eat a lot of grass.

13
00:01:10.297 --> 00:01:15.681
We move often to find water and food.

14
00:01:15.682 --> 00:01:23.362
You have a lot of teeth!

15
00:01:23.363 --> 00:01:29.257
Our teeth help us bite and chew grass.

16
00:01:29.258 --> 00:01:33.538
They never stop growing.

17
00:01:33.539 --> 00:01:36.902
Do you live alone?

18
00:01:36.903 --> 00:01:42.383
No. We stay with our families.

19
00:01:42.384 --> 00:01:47.412
Our families travel in big herds.

20
00:01:47.413 --> 00:01:51.787
Some herds have thousands of zebras!

21
00:01:51.788 --> 00:01:55.532
Why do zebras bite each other?

22
00:01:55.533 --> 00:02:00.912
Zebras don't really bite each other.

23
00:02:00.913 --> 00:02:05.139
We just use our teeth for grooming.

24
00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:10.250
We keep other zebras' coats clean.

25
00:02:10.251 --> 00:02:14.069
I'm thirsty.

26
00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:19.097
It's time to look for water again.

27
00:02:19.098 --> 00:02:27.351
Good-bye, Zebra!
